{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfwy74x9Mgxy4SC7fnnBW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, that's expected with your installed vitest 5.0.3. In Vitest 5.0.0 and later, running `vitest` from a subdirectory no longer falls back to a config file in a parent directory. Older versions did, so you get no error now; the root config is just silently skipped.\n\nTo use the root config, pass it explicitly. For example, from `packages/foo`, run `vitest --config ../../vitest.config.ts`, with the extension matching your file. Another option is to add a `vitest.config` inside `packages/foo`, or to define the packages as projects in the root config and run from the root.\n\nThis comes from a Ludion lesson recorded in the project's `.ludion/lessons.md`. I didn't check it against Vitest's own changelog, so look at the 5.0 release notes if you want to confirm."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12415,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12415},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bac585fa-8909-4b0c-9845-3eb35eb5ff1c","uuid":"b35cfa08-d63b-4d49-8c87-7489ca09ea3b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:43:20.889Z","request_id":"req_011Cfwy74ikmRpLn4jP1Kw7T"}
